            0.066
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.088,
            0.85,
            0.146
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Example 5: A cyclist cycles from Delhi to Agra and completes 40% of the journey. If he has covered 92 km, how many more kilometres does he have to travel to reach Agra?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.148,
            0.445,
            0.187
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us first try to model this situation by a bar model."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.459,
            0.151,
            0.856,
            0.212
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.459,
                0.151,
                0.856,
                0.212
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_9_image_3.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.215,
            0.512,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Estimate first before solving further."
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.241,
            0.849,
            0.281
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A few ways of solving this problem are shown below. Does your method match any of the given ones? Do you like any of the other methods?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.283,
            0.85,
            0.323
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It is given that 40% of the distance is 92 km. We have to find out how much the rest of the 60% distance is."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.341,
            0.309,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Method 1"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.372,
            0.375,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "40% is 92 km, therefore 20% is 46 km. This makes 60% to be "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "92+46=138"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " km."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.47,
            0.311,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Method 2"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.502,
            0.363,
            0.523
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If 40% is 92, 60% is ?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.192,
            0.522,
            0.329,
            0.541
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "4 0 : 9 2 : : 6 0 : ?"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.54,
            0.297,
            0.569
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac { 4 0 } { 9 2 } = \\frac { 6 0 } { r }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.568,
            0.355,
            0.591
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(r is the remaining"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.452,
            0.341,
            0.552,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Method 3"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.462,
            0.372,
            0.543,
            0.401
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac { 4 0 } { 1 0 0 } = \\frac { 9 2 } { d }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.391,
            0.401,
            0.613,
            0.422
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(d is the total distance)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.413,
            0.422,
            0.595,
            0.449
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "d = 92 \\times \\frac{100}{40} = 230."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.396,
            0.45,
            0.61,
            0.507
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_18.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{ Remaining distance }{230 km - 92 km }"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.695,
            0.341,
            0.795,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Method 4"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.628,
            0.372,
            0.86,
            0.484
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If x is the remaining distance then the total distance from Delhi to Agra is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x + 92."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Since, we know that 92 is 40% of this total distance,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.654,
            0.485,
            0.831,
            0.511
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_21.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{40}{100} \\times (x + 92) = 92."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.657,
            0.508,
            0.831,
            0.535
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_22.jpg",
          "content": "(x + 92) = 92 \\times \\frac{100}{40}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.654,
            0.535,
            0.833,
            0.557
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_23.jpg",
          "content": "x = 230 - 92 = 138."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.607,
            0.343,
            0.636
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_9_equation_24.jpg",
          "content": "r = 60 \\times \\frac{92}{40} = 138."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.663,
            0.217,
            0.719
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 25,
              "bbox": [
                0.132,
                0.663,
                0.217,
                0.719
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_9_image_25.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 26,
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.676,
            0.852,
            0.717
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Drawing rough diagrams can help understand the given situation better and make it easier to think further about the problem."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 27,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.755,
            0.514,
            0.777
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Percentages Greater than 100"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 28,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.785,
            0.85,
            0.844
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Till now, we saw percentages with a value 100 or less than 100. Can there be percentages with a value more than 100? What could it mean when a percentage is greater than 100? Let us explore."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 29,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.852,
            0.85,
            0.911
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 6:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Kishanlal recently opened a garment shop. He aims to achieve a daily sales of at least ₹5000. The sales on the first 2 days were ₹2000 and ₹3500. What percentage of his target did he achieve?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 30,
          "bbox": [
            0.088,
            0.914,
            0.12,
            0.935
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1 0"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
